Apply when changing `/track`, `/click`, `/tg/click`, `/openrtb/bid`, filters, parse, gnet, stream producer, local quanta, or edge-tracker alignment.

Reference docs: `docs/PARSER.md`, `docs/TRADEOFFS.md` (hot-path ingest), `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` (hot vs cold). Anti-slop: `anti-slop.mdc`.

## SLA (non-negotiable)

- Handler `ad_http_request_duration_seconds`: p95 < 50 ms, p99 < 80 ms, ceiling 100 ms.
- Production `FILTER_TIMEOUT_MS` <= 100; dev default 5000 ms.
- Redis unified-filter Lua p99 < 10 ms per shard.
- Geo filter p99 < 10 us (sampled).
- `RunAuction` p99 < 15 us; p99 candidates scanned < 500 (`rtb.mdc`).
- Fraud boost snapshot: incremental < 500 us per `FilterEngine.Check`; `BenchmarkFilterFraudBoost` ~90 ns, 0 allocs/op.
- `GetShard` (StaticSlot): ~5.6 ns, 0 allocs/op.
- Load-test abort: control-cohort p99 > 80 ms for 30 s or budget invariant violation.
- Budget invariant: `current_spend <= budget_limit` in Postgres; tests use `AssertBudgetInvariant` (+/-1 micro-unit).
- Financial rule: **fail closed** (503) — never accept spend without debit+log alignment.

## Forbidden on request path (CI-enforced)

`hot_path_static_gate.sh`, `lint_go_hotpath_forbid_gate.sh`, `escape_heap_gate.sh`:

- `defer` inside hot loops (OK at function entry for rare cleanup only if proven 0-alloc).
- Closures that escape or capture per-request variables in filter/parse loops.
- `interface{}` boxing, `sync.Map`, `fmt.Sprintf`, string `+` concat.
- `context.WithValue`, `context.WithTimeout`, `context.WithCancel` on request path.
- Dynamic Prometheus label values computed per event in inner loops.
- `fmt.Errorf` on `/track` — use typed rejects (`filterRejectKind`, `NoBidReason`).
- `json.Marshal` / `encoding/json` on production `/track` or OpenRTB bid response path.
- `net/http` server for tracker ingest (gnet only).
- Import `internal/fraud` ML inference — hot path reads `ml:score:boost:*` snapshot only.
- Synchronous Postgres, ClickHouse, outbox, or external RPC from `processTrack()` or synchronous filter path.

Allowed patterns:

- `sync.Pool` for `Event`, buffers, eval wire, OpenRTB scratch (`handler.go` pools).
- `unsafe.String` / `unsafe.Slice` while gnet frame bytes are valid — copy before async (`evt.StringBuffer`, owned `[]byte`).
- Pre-bound Prometheus counters/histograms with fixed label sets.
- Stack `[N]byte` + `append` with known cap; `strconv.AppendInt` into reused buf.
- `//go:linkname monotonicNano runtime.nanotime` — no `time.Now` in filter deadline loops.

## Data-oriented design (DoD)

Hot path favors **flat data, columnar layout, snapshot readers** over pointer graphs and interface dispatch.

### Structure of Arrays (SoA) — RTB catalog

`internal/rtb/catalog_shard.go`: `CampaignAuctionRegistry` stores parallel slices (`CampaignIDs`, `Bids`, `CTRPPM`, `GeoHashes`, `Weights`, ...). Bucket indices (`GeoBucketStart`, `TargetBucketStart`) point into `candidateBucketSoA` for cache-friendly scans.

Rules:

- Cold rebuild builds new `catalogSnapshot`; publish via `atomic.Pointer[catalogSnapshot].Store`.
- Hot readers: single `loadCatalog()` atomic load per auction — no locks.
- Presorted buckets by score; early break on score floor.
- Geo shard: `req.GeoHash & 63` — 64-way partition.
- Budget CAS in `CheckAndSpendAll` when `RTB_BUDGET_AUTHORITY=rtb`.
- 0 allocs/op in `RunAuction` bench; scan cap p99 < 500 candidates.

### Domain hot models

- `internal/campaignmodel` / hot `internal/domain`: **no struct tags** (no json/db/protobuf on hot structs).
- Registry: `atomic.Pointer` snapshot swap on catalog rebuild; load once per request loop.
- Pad contended atomics: `cpu.CacheLinePad` around MPSC queue heads, breaker counters.

### Sharding — StaticSlot + asm

Production: `StaticSlotSharder` only. `JumpHashSharder` = tests/benches only.

```
slot  = CRC32C(campaign_id) & 1023
shard = slot_table[slot]   // atomic.Value, zero-lock read
```

`internal/domain/sharding_amd64.s`: SSE4.2 `CRC32Q` on two `uint64` limbs of UUID — `NOSPLIT`, ~5.6 ns, 0 allocs. Non-amd64: `hash/crc32` Castagnoli table. **Edge Lua must match** (`edge-slot-map.lua`); parity tests in `sharding_test.go`.

Keys: `{campaign_id}` hash tag so multi-key Lua stays on one master. Never Redis Cluster `MOVED` on hot path.

## Parser and ingress security

Scope: `internal/ingestion` + nginx `edge-phase2.lua`. Full matrix: `docs/PARSER.md`.

### Design goals

1. Reject hostile wire early — **zero allocs on reject path**.
2. Close slow streams — incomplete bodies must not hold connections forever.
3. Edge-tracker parity — same verdict on same wire (`http1IngressCanonical`, `differential_count` must be 0).

### POST /track edge alignment

| Rule | Edge (Lua) | Tracker (gnet) |
| :--- | :---: | :---: |
| `Content-Length` required | yes | yes (`http1TrackEdgePolicy`) |
| Chunked rejected | yes | yes |
| Duplicate/obfuscated `TE` rejected | yes | yes |

Chunked allowed on `POST /openrtb/bid` only (chunk extensions rejected).

Verify: `go test ./internal/ingestion/ -run=TestChaos_CrossHop_NginxGnet -count=1` — `differential_count=0`.

### GET /click

Query-only; `GET` only; strict UUID `campaign_id`. Edge gate: `EDGE_EXPOSE_CLICK`. Shard: CRC32 slot table.

### HTTP/1 slow-stream DoS

| Knob | Default | Behavior |
| :--- | ---: | :--- |
| `HTTP1_INCOMPLETE_MAX` | 3 | Close after N incomplete passes |
| `HTTP1_BODY_IDLE_MS` | 5000 | Wall idle since body expected |
| `MaxRequestBodySize` | 1 MiB | Cap buffered incomplete body |

Metric: `ad_http1_incomplete_close_total{reason}`. H2: `H2_INCOMPLETE_MAX=3`. Operator: nginx `client_body_timeout` at perimeter.

### Framing and wire bombs

- Chunk extensions (`;` in chunk size lines): rejected all paths; hex overflow guard; `chunkScratch` reset; cap > 64 KiB dropped.
- H2 header block: 16 KiB cap (`h2MaxHeaderBlock`) -> `RST_STREAM`.
- TE.TE obfuscation: duplicate `Transfer-Encoding`/`TE`, control chars, tab-obfuscated `chunked` rejected.
- HPACK integer continuation: 8 octet cap (`h2MaxIntContinuationOctets`).
- OpenRTB scan: `ORTB_SCAN_MAX_BYTES=262144`, `ORTB_MAX_QUOTE_CHECKS=65536`; metric `ad_ortb_scan_truncated_total`.
- Protobuf: `PROTO_MAX_FIELDS=256`; pre-scan via `protoWireFieldCount` before `UnmarshalVT` (`proto_wire_budget.go`).
- vtproto hot patch: `make proto` -> `patch-vtproto-hotpath` -> `appendReuseBytes` for repeated bytes (`pb/unmarshal_helpers.go`).

### JSON parse budgets (track / ORTB)

| Constant | Default | Effect |
| :--- | ---: | :--- |
| `MaxJSONTotalWSkip` | 4096 | Cumulative whitespace |
| `MaxJSONStringScanBytes` | 65536 | Bytes in one string |
| `MaxJSONStringEscapes` | 16384 | Escapes per string |
| `MaxJSONKeyPairs` | 10000 | Key:value pairs |
| `MaxJSONDepth` | 16 | Track JSON |
| `OrtbMaxJSONDepth` | 32 | ORTB ingress |
| `JSON_STRICT_UTF8` | on | Reject ill-formed UTF-8 |

Use `jsonScanBudget` (`json_scan_budget.go`) — decrement on ws/string/escape/pair; reject when negative.

### Sustained chaos pass criteria

~90% valid protobuf `/track` + ~10% chaos. Pass: control p99 < 80 ms, `WorkerPoolRejectTotal` delta 0, >=500 control samples.

```bash
bash scripts/fault/parser_chaos_drill.sh
bash scripts/fault/parser_chaos_load.sh --duration=300s --rps=5000 --chaos-pct=10
go test ./internal/ingestion/ -run=TestChaos_ParserSecurity -count=1 -v
```

Chaos tests emit `fault_proof gap=open|closed`.

## gnet HTTP FSM

- HTTP/1.1 DFA on ring buffer — no `net/http` per request.
- `PinnedWorkerPool`: `runtime.LockOSThread()` per worker; route by campaign hash to same core.
- MPSC queues: cache-line padded to avoid false sharing.
- **Async filter offload**: after stream admission `TryReserve`, `FilterEngine.Check` (incl. `EVALSHA`) runs in detached goroutine — pinned workers return to epoll loop immediately. Response written from goroutine; copy `Accept`/`Origin` and event strings before write — no `unsafe.String` over freed frame.
- Microbench reference: HTTP DFA ~539 ns; protobuf ~200 ns; spikes usually Redis/script contention not parse.

## Filter chain order

Execute cheapest first; network last:

```
License -> Emergency Breaker -> Geo -> Schedule -> Segment -> Fraud boost snapshot -> Consent -> UnifiedFilter (Redis Lua)
```

- `FilterDeadlineMono = monotonicNano() + timeout` at entry — **no wall clock** in filter loops.
- `UnifiedFilter` last: only requests that passed all local gates incur Redis RTT.
- Redis breaker open -> 503 `filterRejectInfra` (fail closed).
- Producer overload -> 503 `filterRejectProducerOverload` **before** debit.

## Stream producer, admission, rollback

Layered strategy (`docs/TRADEOFFS.md`):

1. `tryAcquireStreamAdmission` / `TryReserve` at `STREAM_PRODUCER_ADMISSION_PCT` (default 85%) **before** Lua debit.
2. `SetDeferStreamToProducer(true)` -> Lua stream key `fcap:ignored`; single Go writer (`StreamProducer` / `BrokerProducer`).
3. Post-debit enqueue fail -> `budget-rollback.lua` + local quanta ledger refund (200 ms rollback timeout).
4. Local quanta full-skip (`LOCAL_QUOTA_MODE=live`): zero sync `EVALSHA` when eligible; coordinate stream keys to prevent dual `XADD`.

Monitor: `ad_stream_producer_post_debit_rejected_total` should stay ~0; spike = tune admission or capacity.

## Local quanta

- Refill via `local-quota-refill.lua`; debit in Go `TrySpendDebit` (~16 ns).
- Full-skip: local dedup + async publish; eventual consistency on crash — reconciled via refill/return scripts.
- With `StreamProducer`: defer local-quanta stream lane to `fcap:ignored` — one writer.

## BCE, pools, escape analysis

- Length check before indexed loop; `_ = buf[len(buf)-1]` BCE hint when compiler cannot prove bounds.
- Return objects to `sync.Pool` on **all** exit paths (parse reject included).
- After hot-path edits: `make test-alloc-gate`; `go test -run='^$' -bench=. -benchmem ./internal/ingestion/...`.
- `go build -gcflags=-m` on hot packages — no new escapes above `scripts/ci/baselines/escape_hot_path_heap_lines.count`.
- objdump spot-check: no `panicIndex`, `newobject`, `json.*` in inner parse/filter loops.

## GC and runtime tuning (tracker)

- `GOGC=300`, `GOMEMLIMIT` ~700MiB on tracker; processor `GOGC=100`.
- Pre-allocate pools and mmap buffers (GeoIP); avoid per-request heap growth.

## Transport optimizations

- Redis UDS when co-located: `REDIS_ADDRS` unix socket path; dial p50 gate `scripts/perf/redis_uds_benchmark.sh`.
- CPU isolation: `CPU_ISOLATION_ENABLED=1`; verify `scripts/ops/cpu_isolation.sh verify`.

